    "body": "## Problem and change\n\nAfter #6162 moved configuration locks into `HF_HOME`, the unprivileged GB200 test container cannot create them in the shared offline model cache. This blocks main and #6414 before model loading. [Main failure](https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/Megatron-Bridge/actions/runs/38265547949/job/114873855949) and [bump failure](https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/Megatron-Bridge/actions/runs/38266451851/job/114883097920) both report the same lock-file permission error.\n\nFor functional jobs mounting the offline cache, pass the existing `MEGATRON_CONFIG_LOCK_DIR` override to the writable container cache. Every rank in these single-container jobs shares that directory. The shared model cache remains offline; the library default and unit-test configuration are unchanged. This preserves #6162's shared-directory default for multi-node users.\n\nThis is a base CI integration failure introduced by Bridge #6162, independent of the MCore bump. No upstream Megatron-LM PR causes it; the MCore cause taxonomy does not apply.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Regression test executes the actual container-start shell and checks Docker arguments for mounted functional and unmounted unit jobs: **1 failed / 7 passed before; 8 passed after**.\n- Real `safe_load_config_with_retry`, `AutoConfig`, and `FileLock` with an offline local fixture and effective UID 1000: unwritable cache reproduces the permission failure; a writable lock override succeeds.\n- All-file pre-commit and `git diff --check` pass. Independent review found no blocking findings.\n- Requested full L0/L1/L2 CI because the action is shared across the functional matrix. Local evidence does not prove the GPU suite; current-head human review and CI are required before merge.\n",
    "changed_files": 2,
